LAZ_ENGINE_VERSION = 'AmunEV_V2.9'   # LABEL kept at V2.9 (the embedded handover names it; prove_docs checks). EDITS AFTER V2.9 (21 Sep evening, Claude Fable 5.1 — edits only, NOT run, NOT parse-checked, NOT proof-checked by me; the owner's battery is the gate): (1) ESPORTS SETTLEMENT — a tied last-tick score in a no-draw sport is an unrecorded score, not a draw (1,560 of 2,162 matches ended 0-0 in the frame, 74% tied, 781 of 2,088 usable); the CLOSING PRICE settles it (winner <= 1.10, loser >= 3.0: 994 of 1,596 tied matches), the rest UNSETTLED — excluded, never a draw, never a loss (y is NaN without a recorded outcome; before, a leader in a tied match scored as a LOSS: -75% ROI on every rejected chain). (2) FIX B landed for real: both merge keys to [ns] at the bundle's failing merge. (3) PROPOSITIONS writer: the store's bases are tuples, already in rows — TypeError gone. (4) u_drift_opp / u_drift_gap production recipes added (1:1 from the pool; the replay proof failed on the first tick because they had none). (5) Six legacy names (pm_home, pm_away, dog_ml, lead_odds, dp_lead_open, maps_handicap_away) built as aliases and allow-listed — 117 esports book strategies were set aside for them; the supply door reads ONLY FEATURE_PROVENANCE, so they now have hand-written entries there too, and production recipes. (6) The kit's replay proof: production recipes for u_remain and secs_since_price (a new _S.since_price_move clock mirroring the pool: a missing price or the first tick is a move), and a warehouse price/score column (…_odds/_over/_under/_handicap/_home/_away/_draw/_yes/_no, h_score, a_score) passes through as-is via _raw_num instead of being emitted as NaN (away_odds failed that way). (7) price_move_since_score production recipe (_S.ho_at_last_score mirrors the pool's held_since; eTennis replay failed on it). (8) OWNER'S INSTRUCTION: proxy-settled sports (esports, eTennis, tennis, table tennis) are DEPLOYABLE when the verdict passes — settled_by and deployable_reason still name the proxy on every row; LAZ_OWNER['release']['deploy_proxy_settled']=False restores D5. (9) BATCH: the merged kit; each batch child pinned to its own slice (LAZ_FRAME_SOURCE=frame, LAZ_PARQUET_DIR=its folder) — it had been rebuilding its slice from the full raw export. (10) DRAW SPORTS (football, eFootball): final_winner derived from the final recorded score, level = draw — the raw export carries no winner and only no-draw sports were derived, so ensure said NOT READY and every stage raised KeyError. (11) FAIL FAST (runner): a sport whose frame ensure calls NOT READY is not searched; the runner exits non-zero. (12) ONE RULE FOR BOTH DOORS: production recipes derived again over the FINISHED pool, so the supply door stops setting aside book strategies on terms the engine builds. (13) THE BATTERY, FAST: a full battery that passed on these exact engine + runner bytes and environment is not re-run; up to 6 proofs at a time (cores-2; LAZ_AUDIT_WORKERS); slowest first from recorded timings. (14) V2.13 — the inherited doctrine items, read and repaired: the IV term was dead (computed on winners only, wrong-length mask, exception swallowed, 0 for every candidate) — now a real WoE Information Value on the in-sample population; the backstack's swap test was a no-op (an AND is order-independent) — now re-fits the swapped thresholds in the new order; PCA ran in the workers where it never fired, with per-base pc_0 names and an overwritten manifest — now once in the parent, IS-only, content-hashed names, one merged manifest; the monotonicity guard deleted the ladder's LOWER BOUND on a first step down and flattened real U-shapes — now merges only reversals smaller than 1.5 standard errors at the interior edge. THE PERIOD CLOCK (directive 2b/2c): period_idx, prog_period, prog_half, half_idx, league_period_min (NBA 12 / WNBA-FIBA 10 / NCAA men 20-minute halves / HS 8, from the league name), first_goal_prog_half, first_goal_half — research builders, production code and provenance; observation-based (this period's start, the previous period's observed length in this match) because real-basketball minutes are wall time. (15) V2.14 — LONG ODDS, every element that blocked them: the band floor 3 x min_n (300 matches before the search would look; the long-odds bands are the thin ones — esports 176 of 394 attempts died there, the largest at 279) -> 2 x min_n, what the leg gate can actually use (rules.band_min_matches_x); the ladder count 3 x -> 2 x per rung, and the merge keeps the long-odds region (rules.long_odds_from, 4.0) as its own rung(s) whenever it holds the floor instead of folding it into the 1.8+ mass; S3's early stop OFF by default (one barren rung at 1.6 stopped a base's ladder when S2 found no stable set — every base tonight); the registry's band_hi ceiling 50 -> 200 so an open top rung is bounded by the strategy's own range, not an arbitrary number. accept() itself has no win floor and no odds cap (verified). (16) V2.15 — the battery blocked itself: audit_full (CLASS 5, disk reads that never ship) flagged the timings file I added in V2.12; renamed into the audit's runtime-memory class (laz_memory_audit_timings.json). The battery now takes audit360/audit_full from the boot gate's fresh stamp on the same sha instead of running them twice (~6 min per new engine). The launcher names a gate block as a gate block, not '0 passed, 0 failed'. (17) V2.16 — THE ARMING TRACE, rebuilt to arm as the search arms (0/N legs aligned on every run): registry bases were called on scalars and raised (swallowed as 'base not ok'), the period gate read a ctx no caller passed (always period 1), and the trace gated on market_status == Open while the search never does. Now the side/price/armable mask are the search's own arrays (generative store for prop: bases, laz_validate__arm_base otherwise), playability and period are recorded not gating, the band is [lo, hi). The runner passes ctx. THE 2.5-MINUTE FIRST LOAD: every step of laz_frames__load is now