#  LazarusEV_Engine_Generator_v69
#  ONE FILE. Nothing sits beside it.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  WHAT CHANGED FROM v68 -- all three were found by RUNNING it, not by reading it:
#
#  1. EMPTY-ARRAY DRAWDOWN. np.max() on a zero-length array raises "zero-size array to
#     reduction operation maximum which has no identity". SEVENTEEN call sites computed
#     drawdown without checking, so ONE strategy producing no bets aborted the ENTIRE
#     discovered-strategy evaluation -- swallowed by a try/except and reported as a single
#     line while hundreds of strategies were silently skipped. All 17 now route through
#     _laz_maxdd(), which returns 0.0 on empty input. No bets means no drawdown.
#
#  2. lazarus_deployment_spec INLINED. It was a second file that had to sit beside the
#     engine; if it was missing the book built without Deployment_Spec and
#     Feature_Provenance, silently, and a strategy could show 2,109 OOS bets at +153% ROI
#     while being undeployable because nothing downstream knew what made it fire.
#
#  3. MISPLACED __future__ IMPORT. `from __future__ import annotations` sat ~45,000 lines
#     in. It is only legal as a module's FIRST statement, so the file would not compile --
#     while ast.parse() reported OK, because ast does not enforce the rule and the compiler
#     does. Every build check in the previous session passed on a file that could not run.
#     py_compile is used now.
#
#  REGISTRY: 427 strategies, 373 enabled, every one carrying a complete contract.
#  GATES: 14, all passing. Run this file with no arguments to see them.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

