# ── v16 CORRECTNESS FIXES ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  * Draw_Squeeze win_value 'draw' -> 'Draw' (final_result stores 'Draw', so the
#    strategy previously scored ZERO wins). Fixed in STRATEGY_GRID + minimal grid.
#  * Removed the broken shared-memory worker branch. It did
#    `pd.DataFrame(shared.buf)`, which cannot rebuild a mixed-dtype DataFrame from a
#    raw byte buffer, so any worker on that path received garbage. Features are now
#    always serialized once to compact parquet (per-process load, see below).
#  * pandas 3.x compatibility: the VectorizedPool timestamp check used
#    np.issubdtype(dtype, np.number), which raises TypeError on pandas StringDtype.
#    Replaced with pd.api.types.is_numeric_dtype (version-safe on pandas 2.x + 3.x).
#
# ── v16 PERFORMANCE (Phase 3 grid — the dominant cost) ─────────────────────────
#  * Per-PROCESS worker initializer: features load + numpy extraction + the
#    VectorizedPool and strategy masks are built ONCE per worker (ProcessPool
#    `initializer`) instead of once per chunk (~4x per process before).
#  * VectorizedPool precomputes extra_masks only for the ACTIVE strategies
#    (strategy_names=...), not all ~100+ in STRATEGY_GRID.
#  * Batched numba evaluation: _evaluate_variant_numba_multi resolves EVERY odds
#    threshold for a pool in a single _find_triggers_numba pass (one concat + one
#    factorize) instead of re-doing that work per threshold.
#  * Cheap grid pre-filter: VectorizedPool.pool_size() replaces the per-combo
#    full-DataFrame _build_pool copy in the main process.
#
# ── v16 PERFORMANCE (OOS / discovery / reporting) ──────────────────────────────
#  * OOS validation memoizes base pools per (strategy, time_rule, league): each
#    pool is built once per group (holding <=1 OOS + 1 FULL pool at a time — safe
#    on big data) instead of rebuilding full-frame pools for every top-N variant.
#    Results are reassembled in original ranking order (Phase-4 top-20 unchanged).
#  * Greedy discovery builds the base pool once per depth, not per candidate.
#  * calc_opportunity_window pre-filters features to the bet match_ids before the
#    merge (was merging the entire feature frame per detail sheet).
#
# ── VERIFICATION ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Parallel vs serial produce byte-identical raw grid results (full grid, all
#  variants). Batched-numba output is byte-identical to the per-threshold path.
#  End-to-end grid+OOS, discovery, and Excel report all validated under spawn.
