# 1. NEVER put a comma INSIDE the lambda's closing parenthesis:
#      BROKEN:  lambda f: ( (f['x'] > 1), )   ← comma inside = returns TUPLE
#      CORRECT: lambda f: ( (f['x'] > 1) )    ← comma only after OUTER paren
# 2. Every lambda must return a single pd.Series with dtype=bool (not tuple)
# 3. If you add a condition line, the LAST condition has NO trailing comma
# 4. The _self_validate_lambdas() function runs on import and WILL crash
#    with a clear error if you break any lambda. You cannot deploy a broken
#    extra_mask — the script refuses to start.
