#  laz_audit360_run — THE AUDIT LIVES INSIDE THE ENGINE                         [v76_40]
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  The owner's order, 24 Aug: "I HATE standalone scripts that merely fill up the folder
#  and remembering to move files around is an annoying nuisance." So laz_audit360.py is
#  no longer a file to carry -- its full source is embedded below and runs from here.
#
#  THE ENGINEERING LAWS THIS AUDIT ENFORCES, stated where the next model editing this
#  file will read them:
#    1. READ THE ACTUAL FILE before patching it. Never patch from memory of the design.
#    2. ANCHOR COUNT == 1. A replacement whose anchor matches zero or many times is
#       ABORTED, not "applied carefully".
#    3. RUN IT END TO END on real data before shipping. A compile is not a proof.
#    4. EVERY NEW BEHAVIOUR GETS A CHECK. A behaviour with no failing-mode test is a
#       rumour. If a check cannot fail, it is theatre -- delete it.
#    5. WHEN WRONG, REVERT AND SAY SO. The last-tick settlement override (v76_37) is the
#       standing example: it measured 66% at 4.5 odds, was convicted by its own
#       permutation control, and was reverted the same hour.
#
#  HOW IT RUNS SAFELY: the audit seeds ledger rows and writes test books, so running it
#  against a live home would pollute the owner's data. It therefore executes in a SEPARATE
#  PROCESS against a SCRATCH HOME in the system temp dir, deleted afterwards. Nothing it
#  does can reach LAZARUS_HOME.
#
#  WHEN IT RUNS: automatically at startup WHEN THE ENGINE BINARY HAS CHANGED (sha256 of
#  this file vs the last recorded pass), so a new build is verified exactly once and
#  ordinary launches pay nothing. LAZ_SELFTEST=1 forces a run, LAZ_SELFTEST=0 disables,
#  LAZ_SELFTEST_HARD=1 refuses to evolve on any FAIL.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
