# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  v63 SECTION BA — SHORT-FEED VALIDATION (IS/OOS FOCUSED)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Basketball has failed every method here, and the reason is not the method: a 20-day feed split
#  into 6 walk-forward blocks leaves ~3 days per block, which is too thin for a block to mean
#  anything. Demanding 5 of 6 on that feed is demanding noise to behave.
#
#  The honest adaptation is not to lower the bar and pretend nothing changed — it is to use a test
#  the data can actually support, and to LABEL the result as the weaker claim it is.
#
#  SHORT-FEED STANDARD:
#    - 3 walk-forward blocks instead of 6, requiring ALL 3 profitable (stricter per block)
#    - IS/OOS AGREEMENT is promoted to a hard gate: the win-rate gap must be under 4 points and
#      both halves must be individually profitable. This is the test a short feed CAN support.
#    - the bootstrap CI floor and permutation test are unchanged
#
#  A strategy passing this is TIER S — SHORT FEED, never TIER 1/2/3. The distinction is recorded
#  so nobody later reads it as equivalent to a six-block validation.
SHORT_FEED_SPORTS = ('basketball', 'football')
SHORT_FEED_CRITERIA = dict(blocks=3, require_all_blocks=True, max_is_oos_gap=4.0,
                           require_both_halves_positive=True, min_bets_per_half=100)


