    # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # TIER 1 — THE HIGH-ODDS FAMILY. A different market and a different inefficiency
    # from everything above, and the only bar-clearing strategy here at long odds.
    #
    # THE BET: back the team that is CURRENTLY LEADING while the book still prices it as
    # a 3.5-12.0 outsider. That combination is a pre-match underdog that has just taken an
    # early lead (78% of fires are Q1-Q2) against a book that has not repriced it away from
    # its pre-match number. Breakeven at 5.12 is 19.5%; these win 26.8%.
    #
    #   ALL    n=235 wr=26.8% o=5.12 ROI=+35.4% CI95[+5.6,+67.0] maxDD=17.3u  binom p=0.0042
    #   IS     n=121 wr=26.4% o=5.16 ROI=+25.1%                               binom p=0.036
    #   OOS    n=114 wr=27.2% o=5.08 ROI=+46.3%                               binom p=0.033
    #   FREEZE n= 56 wr=30.4% o=4.96 ROI=+55.7%                               binom p=0.046
    #   SELECT n= 70 wr=22.9% o=5.19 ROI=+31.9%                               binom p=0.26
    #   weekly +37% / +25% / +24% / +79%; 90 leagues; leave-out-top-3 ROI +27.6%
    #
    # BAND SELECTION WAS HELD OUT. The 3.5-12.0 band is the argmax of a 16-cell scan run
    # on the FIT window ALONE (earliest 40% of matches). FREEZE and SELECT played no part
    # in choosing it and both came back positive. That is the strongest evidence in this
    # file, and it is why this ships enabled while several higher-ROI stacks above do not.
    #
    # WHAT TO BE CAREFUL ABOUT — this is a longshot strategy and behaves like one:
    #   · 63 wins in 235 bets. The full-sample CI is [+5.6,+67.0]; on the clean
    #     FREEZE+SELECT windows it is [-1.5,+88.6], which just touches zero. The edge
    #     looks real; its MAGNITUDE is very poorly determined.
    #   · SELECT alone is not significant (p=0.26). Only the combination is.
    #   · Expect long losing runs. Max drawdown 17.3u came on a +83u total.
    #   · Full-Kelly f* = 9.0%; quarter-Kelly = 2.3% of bank. Do not exceed that on a
    #     26.8% strike rate.
    #   · A permutation null that shuffles wins WITHIN odds deciles is uninformative for
    #     this family (it preserves the win count per odds bin, which is what generates the
    #     ROI: null mean +34.2% vs observed +35.4%). The correct test is the binomial
    #     against the book's own vig-stripped implied probability, quoted above.
    #   · UNVERIFIABLE FROM THIS FEED: whether a book will lay meaningful size on a live
    #     in-play moneyline at 5-12. Shadow first and record fill rates, not just prices.
    # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
