# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  LAZARUSEV DOCUMENTATION CONTRACT — v1 — BINDING ON EVERY VERSION FROM v67 ONWARD
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#  THE RULE
#  ────────
#  A betting strategy that cannot be re-created from its own documentation is not a
#  strategy. It is a number. No strategy may be enabled in any version of this engine
#  unless every element below is recorded in text sufficient for an engineer who has never
#  seen the research to rebuild it exactly, in real time, from the production feed alone.
#
#  This is not a style guide. laz_documentation_gate() enforces it, and a strategy that
#  fails it must not be promoted past shadow mode regardless of how good its metrics look.
#
#  WHY THIS EXISTS
#  ───────────────
#  The eFootball inverse family carried 30 enabled strategies reporting 76-77% win rates
#  for months. When they were finally traced, the win rate turned out to be an artefact of
#  pandas groupby.first() splicing values from different ticks into an entry row that never
#  existed at any single instant. Ten of sixteen produced ZERO bets once corrected.
#
#  The reason it survived so long is that the registry recorded `conditions` and
#  `condition_values` but NOT: which tick the bet was struck on, how each feature was
#  computed, what the entry row was reduced from, or which base signal an inverse spec had
#  flipped. Every one of those omissions was individually reasonable. Together they made a
#  live book unauditable.
#
#  Nine further defects were found in the same audit. EVERY ONE FAILED CLOSED — no
#  exception, no log line, just "no qualifying matches":
#     1. groupby.first() composite entry rows
#     2. suspended quotes counted as placeable bets
#     3. odds floor applied outside the universe, so thresholds were fitted on unbettable rows
#     4. forward-looking price persistence (look-ahead)
#     5. row-shift vs observed-price stability semantics diverging between backtest and live
#     6. float32 odds boundary at exactly 1.90 rejecting prices the backtest accepted
#     7. `hour` absent from the live engine — every hour-gated strategy fired zero bets
#     8. float('nan') is not None — NaN poisoned the running price extremes
#     9. the evaluator iterating one registry list instead of all of them
#  A silent failure is the expensive kind. Documentation is how it is caught before it ships.
#
#  THE SEVEN ELEMENTS — every strategy, every version
#  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  1. IDENTITY      name, laz_id, sport, family, tier, engine version, enabled state.
#
#  2. MARKET        which market is backed, in the book's own words, and WHICH SIDE.
#                   "total_goals_under" is not enough; "back the UNDER on the full-match
#                   total goals line quoted at entry" is. For a moneyline, name the player
#                   or team selection rule ("the player who won the FIRST SET").
#
#  3. TICK          the exact tick the bet is struck on, stated as a rule a machine can
#                   follow: "the FIRST tick at which every condition holds, one bet per
#                   (match, strategy), never revised." Say what the entry row is reduced
#                   from — nth(0), NEVER first(). Say the placeability window.
#
#  4. FEATURES      for EVERY feature in the conditions:
#                     · what it means in one plain sentence
#                     · the exact source column(s) in the production table
#                     · the backtest expression, verbatim
#                     · the live expression, verbatim
#                     · its NaN policy, stated as behaviour ("fails closed, no trigger")
#                     · any in-match state it needs and from WHEN (kick-off? halftime?)
#                     · any parity risk between the fitted and live forms
#                   If the backtest and live expressions are not both written down and
#                   identical in meaning, the strategy is not documented.
#
#  5. CONDITIONS    every condition in plain English AND as a machine-readable string,
#                   joined by AND, never OR, with the economic reason the condition exists.
#                   A threshold with no stated reason is a fitted number, not a signal.
#
#  6. SETTLEMENT    what makes the bet win, referencing the value QUOTED AT ENTRY, never a
#                   closing line. If the outcome is derived rather than read from a column
#                   — as tennis is, from the final-odds collapse — say so, give the rule,
#                   and give the measured accuracy of that derivation.
#
#  7. EVIDENCE      IS and OOS bet counts, win rates, ROI, mean odds, max drawdown, the
#                   split rule that produced them, and the KNOWN LIMITS: sample size,
#                   correlation with other registered strategies, and anything about the
#                   data that will not hold in production.
#
#  THREE THINGS THAT MUST ALWAYS BE WRITTEN DOWN
#  ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#  · ATTACHMENT. Any feature anchored on the first tick of a match (opening line, opening
#    price, running extremes, latched winners) is WRONG if the collector joined late. Say
#    which features need attachment and what to do when it is missing: drop the match.
#  · CORRELATION. If registered strategies draw from the same pool, say so and say to size
#    them as one position. Sixteen specs over 209 matches is one position, not sixteen.
#  · WHAT WILL CHANGE. Off-season league mixes, sample-median features, whitelists fitted
#    on one period. If a number will move when the data moves, that belongs in the record.
#
#  BANNED FROM ANY CONDITION, PERMANENTLY
#  ──────────────────────────────────────
#  · Sample-derived statistics (line_rel = line/median(line) and anything like it). They
#    look like match state and are really a proxy for whatever happened to be in the
#    sample. Use absolute thresholds.
#  · League names for sports where leagues do not recur in volume. Synthetic formats only.
#  · Any quantity unknowable at bet time: total ticks in the match, the final score, a
#    future price. If it cannot be computed from this tick plus state held since kick-off,
#    it cannot be in a condition.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

LAZ_DOC_CONTRACT_VERSION = 'laz-doc-contract-1'

LAZ_DOC_REQUIRED_STRATEGY_FIELDS = (
    'name', 'sport', 'family', 'market', 'min_odds', 'conditions', 'metrics', 'note',
)
# Every metrics dict must name the dataset its numbers came from. A metric without
# provenance cannot be reproduced or challenged, and the audit found 36 of 61 strategies
# missing it because it was added by hand per family instead of enforced.
LAZ_DOC_REQUIRED_METRIC_FIELDS = ('measured_on',)


def laz_stamp_provenance(strategies, measured_on, overwrite=False):
    """Stamp `measured_on` onto every metrics dict. Call this at the END of any block that
    registers strategies -- it is cheaper than remembering, and the gate rejects anything
    that slips through."""
    n = 0
    for s in strategies:
        m = s.setdefault('metrics', {})
        if overwrite or not m.get('measured_on'):
            m['measured_on'] = measured_on
            n += 1
    return n
LAZ_DOC_REQUIRED_LINEAGE_FIELDS = (
    'definition', 'source_cols', 'formula', 'live_expr', 'nan_policy',
)


def laz_windowed_feature_declared(feature, lineage):
    """True if `feature` is not windowed, or is windowed AND declares its semantics.
    laz_window_semantics_gate AUDITS the lineage; this BLOCKS the registration."""
    r = lineage.get(feature)
    if r is None:
        return False
    if feature not in laz_detect_windowed_features({feature: r}):
        return True
    return str(r.get(LAZ_DOC_REQUIRED_WINDOW_FIELD, '')).lower().strip() \
        in LAZ_WINDOW_SEMANTICS_VALUES


def laz_documentation_gate(strategies, lineage, condition_re, out=print,
                           require_backtest_expr=True):
    """THE gate. A strategy that fails this must not be enabled.

    Checks, per strategy:
      · every required field is present and non-empty
      · every condition parses to feature/operator/threshold
      · every feature has a lineage record
      · every lineage record carries all five required fields
      · the record names its source columns and BOTH expressions

    Returns (ok, failures). Wire into the promotion path so an undocumented strategy
    physically cannot reach production.
    """
    failures = []
    for s in strategies:
        nm = s.get('name', '<unnamed>')
        for fld in LAZ_DOC_REQUIRED_STRATEGY_FIELDS:
            if not s.get(fld):
                failures.append(f'{nm}: missing strategy field `{fld}`')
        for fld in LAZ_DOC_REQUIRED_METRIC_FIELDS:
            if not (s.get('metrics') or {}).get(fld):
                failures.append(f'{nm}: metrics missing `{fld}` — the numbers cannot be '
                                f'reproduced without naming the dataset they came from')
        for c in s.get('conditions', []):
            g = condition_re.match(c)
            if not g:
                failures.append(f'{nm}: condition `{c}` does not parse')
                continue
            feat = g.group(1)
            rec = lineage.get(feat)
            if rec is None:
                failures.append(f'{nm}: feature `{feat}` has NO lineage record — '
                                f'cannot be re-created')
                continue
            for fld in LAZ_DOC_REQUIRED_LINEAGE_FIELDS:
                if not rec.get(fld):
                    failures.append(f'{nm}: `{feat}` lineage missing `{fld}`')
            # WINDOWED FEATURES MUST DECLARE HOW THEIR WINDOW COUNTS. u_flat reached
            # production-candidate status with a 40-observation window that could never fill
            # inside its own p<=0.45 entry window -- 66 bets in the backtest, ZERO live --
            # because nothing stopped it at REGISTRATION time. This does.
            if not laz_windowed_feature_declared(feat, lineage):
                failures.append(f'{nm}: feature `{feat}` is WINDOWED but does not declare '
                                f'`{LAZ_DOC_REQUIRED_WINDOW_FIELD}` — a window counted in '
                                f'rows has a length that depends on collector poll rate, so '
                                f'backtest and live will silently disagree')
            # WINDOWED FEATURES MUST DECLARE HOW THEIR WINDOW COUNTS. The window gate audits
            # the lineage; THIS blocks the registration. u_flat reached production-candidate
            # status with a 40-observation window that could never fill inside its own entry
            # window -- 66 bets in the backtest, ZERO live -- because nothing stopped it here.
            if 'laz_windowed_feature_declared' in globals() \
                    and not laz_windowed_feature_declared(feat, lineage):
                failures.append(f'{nm}: feature `{feat}` is WINDOWED but does not declare '
                                f'`{LAZ_DOC_REQUIRED_WINDOW_FIELD}` — a window counted in '
                                f'rows has a length that depends on collector poll rate, so '
                                f'backtest and live will silently disagree')
            if require_backtest_expr and not rec.get('backtest_expr'):
                failures.append(f'{nm}: `{feat}` has no backtest_expr — backtest and live '
                                f'cannot be shown to agree')
    ok = not failures
    if out:
        out(f'[doc gate {LAZ_DOC_CONTRACT_VERSION}] {len(strategies)} strategies — '
            f'{"PASS" if ok else f"FAIL ({len(failures)} problems)"}')
        for f in failures[:25]:
            out(f'    {f}')
        if len(failures) > 25:
            out(f'    ... and {len(failures)-25} more')
    return ok, failures



# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  v67 — eFOOTBALL WHITELIST-BASE UNDER FAMILY                               [ADDITIVE]
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  ALL TEN ARE TIER 1 - OMEGA: 100+ bets, 65%+ strike, +5 edge, positive ROI AND bootstrap
#  CI floor in ALL FIVE segments (IS, OOS, forward, backward, freeze), 6/6 walk-forward
#  blocks, permutation p < 0.005 against the parent universe.
#
#  ── WHY THIS FAMILY EXISTS, AND WHAT IT REPLACES ────────────────────────────────────
#  The earlier efb_totals_under and efb_totals_under_poisson families were fitted across
#  ALL eight eFootball leagues. Three of those leagues are badly mispriced and five are
#  close to efficient, so a threshold tuned on the pooled average fits neither. Bolting
#  `wl >= 1` onto those strategies afterwards intersects two populations chosen for
#  different reasons and gains only 0.5-6.5 win-rate points.
#
#  Searching FROM the whitelist finds conditions that work INSIDE those three leagues.
#  Same feature vocabulary, different base:
#      old book best   66.8% WR  o=2.06  +37.7% ROI
#      this family     75.8-80.9% WR  o=2.05-2.39  +64.9% to +83.8% ROI
#  +14 win-rate points, +0.3 odds, roughly double the ROI. The cost is volume: the
#  whitelist base at odds>=2.00 is 9,741 matches and these select 301-581 each.
#
#  ── THE WHITELIST ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Frozen, fitted on the IS half only, then applied to OOS:
#      eFootball H2H CG League - 8 mins play    IS ROI +40.3%
#      eFootball Valkyrie Cup - 8 mins play     IS ROI +29.6%
#      eFootball Valhalla Cup - 8 mins play     IS ROI +27.8%
#  Excluded, and they were dragging every earlier number down:
#      Battle - Volta League 6 mins  +6.3%   Battle - 12 mins  +2.4%
#      Battle - 8 mins play          +2.2%   GT Leagues        -0.6%
#      Adriatic League               -3.2%
#  The 10/15/20/25% cut-offs all select the same three, so nothing hinges on where the
#  line is drawn. THIS IS A BET THAT THOSE THREE FORMATS STAY MISPRICED -- re-fit monthly.
#  League whitelisting is valid here ONLY because these leagues recur in volume (8 leagues
#  averaging 2,400 matches). It is banned for real football and basketball, where 565 and
#  167 leagues average 5 matches each.
#
#  ── ENTRY, PLACEABILITY, ATTACHMENT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  FIRST tick where all conditions hold; one bet per (match, strategy); entry row is
#  groupby('match_id').nth(0), NEVER .first(). Median entry sits at 50-75% of the match --
#  every one is inside the prog <= 0.80 placeability window, because books close in-play
#  betting late. u_rank, u_drift and u_flat are anchored on the opening price: a match
#  first seen after kick-off must be DROPPED, not bet.
#
#  ── CORRELATION ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Seven of the ten use a `prog` term and will fire on overlapping ticks. The two WITHOUT
#  one -- Cheap_NearLine_Margin and PoissonEdge_NearLine_Margin -- enter earlier and are
#  the genuine diversifiers. Size the prog-gated seven as one position.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

