# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  v67 — eFOOTBALL COMEBACK (LOSER) FAMILY                                   [ADDITIVE]
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  BACK THE SIDE THAT IS CURRENTLY LOSING, TO WIN THE MATCH OUTRIGHT.
#
#  ── THIS IS THE MASTER BOOK'S LARGEST eFOOTBALL FAMILY, AND IT WAS MISSED ──────────
#  23 of 56 eFootball specs in LazarusEV_MASTER_BOOK carry market="loser". Every one of
#  them whitelists EXACTLY GT Leagues and Adriatic League. Those are the two leagues an
#  earlier pass in this project declared unexploitable -- because it tested only the
#  TOTALS market there, found -1.6% under and -16.5% over, and stopped. Static "back home"
#  and "back away" were also tested (-11.0%, -14.1%) and also rejected. The book does not
#  bet home or away; it bets whoever is BEHIND at that tick, which is a different bet
#  entirely and was never measured until now.
#
#  ── WHY THESE TWO LEAGUES ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  They are the LONGEST formats in the feed: GT Leagues 12 minutes, Adriatic 10, against
#  8 minutes for every whitelist-under league. More time to score is exactly why their
#  totals are correctly priced AND why their comeback market is not: the book prices a
#  one-goal deficit as near-fatal when there is still half a match to play.
#
#  ── MEASURED, trailing side, trail_by<=1 ────────────────────────────────────────────
#      odds>=8  base    7,642 bets   8.7% WR   +51.4% ROI
#      odds>=12 base    5,424 bets   6.5% WR   +25.1% ROI
#  Conditioned, the same universe reaches 19-21% WR at odds 20-24 with +270% to +380% ROI.
#
#  ── `jump` IS NOT IN THIS FAMILY, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE ────────────────────────────
#  Four earlier entries used jump >= 4.0. On a universe rebuilt from raw CSV carrying BOTH
#  sides' prices per tick, jump does not appear in the top 14 single conditions at all. It
#  had ranked highly only under a BROKEN anchor: an earlier build divided by the first tick
#  of the TRAILING SERIES, which mixes two different players' opening prices whenever the
#  lead changes hands. That manufactured signal. The corrected per-side anchor removes it.
#  Every condition registered below is one the live engine provably computes -- verified by
#  feeding a synthetic tick through V67CbFeatureEngine and checking each value.
#
#  ── THE EDGE EXISTS ONLY ABOVE ODDS ~14. MEASURED, DO NOT RE-SEARCH BELOW IT. ───────
#  Raw comeback rate vs the price's implied rate, trail_by<=1, by band:
#      odds  2-4   n=3,179  implied 32.0%  actual 24.1%  edge -7.9  ROI -24.8%
#      odds  4-6   n=5,115  implied 21.5%  actual 17.1%  edge -4.4  ROI -20.2%
#      odds  6-8   n=3,847  implied 15.3%  actual 11.5%  edge -3.7  ROI -24.2%
#      odds  8-11  n=3,886  implied 11.5%  actual  8.9%  edge -2.6  ROI -21.5%
#      odds 11-14  n=2,599  implied  8.4%  actual  7.4%  edge -1.0  ROI -10.8%
#      odds 14-20  n=2,414  implied  6.3%  actual  6.7%  edge +0.4  ROI  +8.0%
#      odds 20+    n=4,070  implied  3.2%  actual  3.5%  edge +0.4  ROI  +4.6%
#  The book is CORRECT below 14 and wrong above it. Every entry registered here sits at a
#  10.0+ floor for that reason. Exhaustive 2-, 3- and 4-way searches over 28 conditions in
#  the 4-9 band returned ZERO candidates at 26% win rate; the best subsets there merely
#  select a thin positive pocket inside a structurally negative population.
#  min_rest_min is 0% populated in this feed, so the book's rest_max specs cannot be built.
#
#  ── THE PROFILE IS NOT THE UNDER BOOK. READ IT BEFORE SIZING. ───────────────────────
#  Max consecutive LOSSES runs 10-39. Max consecutive WINS is 2-3. Wins arrive scattered,
#  not clustered. V67_CB_Jump_Scoring is the only entry where one winner covers the worst
#  drawdown (24.00 odds vs 10u). Flat small stakes; this is not a strike-rate instrument.
#
#  ── SIGNED FEATURES: DIRECTION IS THE WHOLE POINT ───────────────────────────────────
#  An earlier pass computed elo_gap and wr_gap as ABSOLUTE differences, which says there
#  is a mismatch but not WHO is behind. The comeback thesis needs the STRONGER player to
#  be the one trailing. Rebuilt signed to the trailing side, elo_adv_loser >= 0 alone
#  lifts the base from 7.9% to 16.9% WR and from +33.9% to +179.5% ROI -- more than every
#  price-and-pace condition combined.
