# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  v67 — UNIVERSAL UPLIFT LAYER                                              [ADDITIVE]
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  ONE FUNCTION, EVERY STRATEGY, EVERY SPORT. laz_uplift() takes a registered strategy and
#  tries each lever this project measured, keeping only what improves BOTH halves. It does
#  not invent conditions; it applies known, documented, per-sport-tested modifications.
#
#  THE LEVERS, AND WHAT EACH WAS MEASURED TO BE WORTH
#  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  1. PLACEABILITY CAP  prog <= 0.80
#     Books close in-play betting late. Two real-football strategies fired at median prog
#     0.98 and 1.00 -- 92% and 98% of their bets unplaceable. Capping did not merely make
#     them legal, it RAISED the survivors, because the late bets were the losing ones:
#         line>=3.5 AND h_tp<=0          77.9% -> 88.0% WR   +58.2% -> +70.9% ROI
#         u_rank<=0.3 AND h_tp<=0 AND .. 70.8% -> 82.0% WR   +36.1% -> +57.1% ROI
#     APPLIES TO: every sport. Free win rate wherever a strategy enters late.
#
#  2. LEAGUE WHITELIST  wl >= 1
#     The single largest lever found. Synthetic sports only -- it needs leagues that recur
#     in volume. eFootball has 8 leagues averaging 2,400 matches; real football has 565
#     averaging 5, real basketball 167 averaging 5, and structural grouping on those came
#     back negative in every bucket.
#         eFootball base 56.8% WR / +10.7% ROI  ->  whitelist 67.7% / +33.7%
#         eBasketball whitelist   IS 88.2% / OOS 91.6% WR / +73.8% ROI
#     CRITICAL: search FROM the whitelist, do not bolt it on. Bolting it onto strategies
#     fitted across all leagues gains 0.5-6.5 points; searching from it gains +14.
#
#  3. TIGHT PRICE INACTIVITY  u_flat <= 0.03-0.05
#     The master book's Conditions_Legend calls market inactivity "the single strongest
#     signal in this book" and uses 0.03-0.05. An earlier pass used 0.15-0.30, five times
#     looser. Measured on eFootball:
#         u_flat <= 0.03  63.9% WR / +24.8% ROI      u_flat <= 0.15  60.2% / +15.4%
#     APPLIES TO: any totals strategy in any sport.
#
#  4. OVERREACTION  jump family
#     Current price / a reference price, computed PER SELECTION every tick and aligned to
#     role afterwards. Direction is a property of the MARKET:
#         backing a comeback -> want the price moved AWAY from us (fade the overreaction)
#         backing an under   -> want it moved TOWARD us (follow the confirmation)
#     Only pays where the strategy has NO other price-movement term. On the eFootball
#     whitelist unders, which are built on u_rank/u_drift/u_flat, it improved 3 of 10 and
#     only as a co-condition (keep both), never as a replacement:
#         PriceSteady + u_jump <= 1.10   79.0% -> 80.7% WR, +65.1% -> +68.7%, 95% of volume
#     And it is INERT where the odds floor already implies it: at odds>=10 in the comeback
#     market, 97-100% of trailing sides have already jumped, so jump cannot discriminate.
#
#  5. SIGNED, ROLE-RELATIVE FEATURES
#     An absolute difference (|elo_home - elo_away|) says a mismatch exists but not WHO is
#     ahead. Rebuilt signed to the backed side, elo_adv_loser >= 0 alone lifted the
#     comeback base from 7.9% to 16.9% WR and +33.9% to +179.5% ROI -- more than every
#     price-and-pace condition combined. APPLIES TO: any strategy backing one of two sides.
#
#  6. ABSOLUTE THRESHOLDS, NEVER SAMPLE MEDIANS
#     line_rel = line_open / median(line_open) looks like match state and is a league proxy:
#     when the league mix changes the median moves and every threshold shifts with it.
#     Replacing it with an absolute cut both survives the change AND performs better:
#         football   best OOS 55.2% / +13.1%  ->  88.0% / +70.9%   (line >= 3.5)
#         basketball best OOS 69.0% / +22.8%  ->  70.4% / +27.8%   (line >= 175)
#
#  WHAT laz_uplift DOES NOT DO
#  ───────────────────────────
#  It will not add a lever that fails to improve BOTH halves, will not accept a volume loss
#  beyond min_volume_frac, and will not apply a sport-inappropriate lever (no league
#  whitelist on real football, no jump where a price-movement term already exists).
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

LAZ_UPLIFT_LEVERS = {
    'placeability':  dict(applies=('efootball', 'football', 'ebasketball', 'basketball', 'tennis'),
                          cond='prog <= 0.80',
                          why='books close in-play betting late; late bets are also the losing ones'),
    'whitelist':     dict(applies=('efootball', 'ebasketball', 'tennis'),
                          cond='wl >= 1',
                          why='synthetic sports only; needs leagues that recur in volume'),
    'flat_tight':    dict(applies=('efootball', 'football', 'ebasketball', 'basketball'),
                          cond='u_flat <= 0.05',
                          why='market inactivity, measured at the book\'s own threshold'),
    'jump_confirm':  dict(applies=('efootball', 'ebasketball'),
                          cond='u_jump <= 1.10',
                          why='under price has not drifted out; only where no other price-movement term exists'),
    'overround':     dict(applies=('efootball', 'football', 'ebasketball', 'basketball', 'tennis'),
                          cond='overround <= 1.10',
                          why='tighter book margin; nearly free, rarely cuts volume'),
}




