#
#  THE EDGE GROWS WITH THE ODDS: +35.8 points at a 1.70 floor rising to +41.6 at 2.00.
#  That is the opposite of the usual pattern -- normally a higher floor buys longer prices
#  at a lower strike. Here the whitelist leagues hold their win rate as the price lengthens,
#  so the high-odds end is the MOST profitable, not the least.
#
#  Each layer is independent and additive: the base is the totals line running high, the
#  wall is the pair's own scoring history, the whitelist is which leagues misprice. None of
