V67_FEATURE_LINEAGE_FULL['fb_pace'] = dict(V67_FEATURE_LINEAGE_FULL['pace'])
V67_FEATURE_LINEAGE_FULL['fb_pace'].update(
    definition='the current scoring pace of a 90-MINUTE football match, extrapolated to a full '
               'match: total goals divided by the elapsed fraction of 90 minutes.',
    formula='total_goals / (minute / 90)',
    backtest_expr='tg / np.maximum(fb_prog, 0.10)',
    live_expr='(h_score + a_score) / max(S.minute/90.0, 0.10)',
    source_cols=['h_score', 'a_score', 'phase'], units='goals per match',
    note='THE ONE FEATURE IN THE FOOTBALL OVER BOOK THAT IS NOT HALF-TIME BASED, and it '
         'appears in five of the eight entries. '
         'fb_pace <= 2 combined with ht_tot >= 2 is a deliberate contradiction: the match '
         'scored TWICE OR MORE before the break, but the pace has since FALLEN below two goals '
         'per match-equivalent. The book holds the total high because the goals already came; '
         'the match has actually gone quiet. That disagreement between what HAS happened and '
         'what IS happening carries the strongest entry in the football registry -- 86.0% '
         'out-of-sample on a 2.1u drawdown. '
         'Named fb_pace rather than the bare `pace` to avoid the cross-sport namespace '
         'collision the audit enforces. The denominator is 90 minutes here; eFootball uses '
         '8-12 and eBasketball a 5-minute quarter, so the same arithmetic means something '
         'entirely different in each sport.')


