#  WHY THE MONEYLINE SIDE WAS NEVER SEARCHED BEFORE. bb66_universe applied one odds band --
#  1.70 to 2.20 -- to every market. That band was chosen for TOTALS, where both sides sit
#  near even money. A trailing basketball side prices at 3 to 15, so EVERY moneyline row
#  failed the filter and the search never saw the market at all. Not empty: deleted.
#  The band is now per-market and floor-only, per the owner's specification.
#
#  PERMUTATION CONTROL: 1 real :: [0, 0, 0] null. Three independent runs of the identical
#  search on shuffled outcomes found nothing. The stack is not an artefact of searching
#  2500 times.
#
#  THE FREEZE READING IS THE RISK, AND IT IS RECORDED HERE SO IT CANNOT BE FORGOTTEN.
#      IS  106 / +29.3      OOS 107 / +22.4      FREEZE 64 / +5.3
#  FREEZE is the middle 30% of matches and no selection step could read it. Most of the
#  measured edge sits in the two windows the search had access to. Compare BBQ12 on the
#  under side: FREEZE +24.3, losing run 3, drawdown 4.2u. This is a different instrument.
#
#  THE SHAPE OF THE BET. 32.9% strike at 4.70 means most bets lose and the return comes
#  from a minority of large wins. The longest losing run IN THE MEASURED SAMPLE is 11.
#  Expect to see it again. The confidence interval runs +0.2% to +52.9% -- 213 bets cannot
#  separate "barely profitable" from "very profitable", so treat the point estimate as one
#  draw from a wide distribution, not as the number.
#
#  POLL-RATE DEPENDENCY. u_flat is abs(u - u 40 ROWS ago), a row window, not a clock
#  window. If production polls at a different cadence than the CSV, this fires at different
#  moments than the backtest. Match the row count, not a duration.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

