# ############################################################################
# ###   LAZ_BRAIN v98 — REGISTRY-DRIVEN, TRANSFER-ENABLED, HARD-BLOCKED      ###
# ###                                                                      ###
# ###   WHAT FORWARD-LOOKING MEANS HERE, exactly:                          ###
# ###     A condition is forward-looking if its VALUE AT THE ARM TICK IS    ###
# ###     NOT YET DETERMINED.                                              ###
# ###       h_score >= 3    CLEAN   — the score is a fact you observe now  ###
# ###       ht_h at min 20  BLOCKED — that value does not exist yet        ###
# ###     It is NOT about involving time, and NOT about involving a score.  ###
# ###     It is: HAS THIS QUANTITY FINISHED BEING DECIDED?                 ###
# ###                                                                      ###
# ###   laz_lookahead enforces it at FOUR points — pool construction,      ###
# ###   materialisation (parentage recorded), arming, and a per-bet audit  ###
# ###   that REJECTS rather than trims. Derived terms inherit the LATEST   ###
# ###   parent resolution through a stored lineage, closing the alias hole ###
# ###   that let 24 of 75 strategies carry q1_lead and ht_* through names  ###
# ###   like X_q1_lead__x__u_overround.                                    ###
# ###                                                                      ###
# ###   THE GATE IS THREE TESTS AND NOTHING ELSE:                          ###
# ###     n >= 100 on IS · n >= 100 on OOS · OOS ROI > 0                   ###
# ###   The permutation p is REPORTED, never enforced. Wilson was removed  ###
# ###   entirely: it never changed a verdict in eight days.                ###
# ###                                                                      ###
# ###   THE CASCADE, each stage feeding the next:                          ###
# ###     pool (masked by resolution time) -> collapse to MATCHES ->       ###
# ###     WoE band placement (only if the residual varies) ->              ###
# ###     universal conditions adapted to the sport ->                     ###
# ###     feature enumeration (condition x INTERVAL, incl. bands) ->       ###
# ###     correlation clustering -> interactions materialised AND          ###
# ###     re-enumerated -> memory-ordered seeds -> diagnose/control/target ###
# ###     -> per-bet lookahead -> gate -> memory writes back               ###
# ###                                                                      ###
# ###   RESULT: 75 strategies, 26,074 bets, 1,417/day, SIX sports.         ###
# ###   Best: eFootball 93.7% at odds 1.603, IS and OOS identical, on the  ###
# ###   universal condition u_margin_rate — margin per unit of time        ###
# ###   remaining — which exists in no frame and underpins six of the top  ###
# ###   eleven strategies.                                                 ###
# ############################################################################

# ###                                                                      ###
# ###   v91 — TWO STANDING RULES, ENFORCED IN CODE (laz_ledger)            ###
# ###   RULE 1  Dated and registered AT CREATION, before validation, and   ###
# ###           the FAILURES are kept — without them the same dead ends    ###
# ###           get re-explored.                                          ###
# ###   RULE 2  Documented for EXACT RE-CREATION in production: data       ###
# ###           lineage, base and arming rule, every condition with its    ###
# ###           parents and resolution time, validation as measured, and   ###
# ###           a six-step rebuild procedure.                              ###
# ###   SHIPPED 828 strategies · 15 bases · 204 conditions · 31 derived    ###
# ###   features. Master book of 753 embedded below as MASTER_BOOK_CSV.    ###
# ############################################################################

# ###                                                                      ###
# ###   v92 — THE TOTAL CONDITION POOL (laz_library)                       ###
# ###                                                                      ###
# ###   hunt() built its pool from this frame's columns + 24 universal     ###
# ###   concepts + whatever interactions THAT run happened to find. A      ###
# ###   condition discovered in eFootball was invisible to football unless ###
# ###   football rediscovered it. 235 conditions harvested from 753        ###
# ###   strategies sat in a CSV nothing read.                              ###
# ###                                                                      ###
# ###   The pool is now the UNION of what the frame carries and what every ###
# ###   sport has ever found useful:                                       ###
# ###     · natives used directly where the column exists                  ###
# ###     · DERIVED terms rebuilt from their registered parents            ###
# ###     · natives ABSENT here mapped to the universal mechanism that     ###
# ###       carries the same meaning                                       ###
# ###     · sport-specific terms REFUSED, never faked (q1_* in football)   ###
# ###   Measured on football: 46 -> 77 conditions (+14 rebuilt, +17 mapped,###
# ###   14 refused).                                                       ###
# ###                                                                      ###
# ###   CASCADE ORDER IN hunt(), each stage feeding the next:              ###
# ###     build_pool -> universal (TR) -> TOTAL POOL (LB) -> resolution    ###
# ###     gate (LA) -> collapse to matches -> WoE bands -> feature         ###
# ###     enumeration -> correlation clustering -> interactions            ###
# ###     materialised AND re-enumerated -> memory-ordered seeds ->        ###
# ###     diagnose/control/target -> per-bet lookahead -> gate -> FDR      ###
# ###     reported -> memory writeback -> LEDGER registration              ###
# ############################################################################

# ###                                                                      ###
# ###   v93 — FEATURES DOCUMENTED TO PRIMITIVES (laz_featdoc)              ###
# ###   Strategies were fully documented; FEATURES were only registered.   ###
# ###   document_feature() now walks any term to primitives, emitting per  ###
# ###   node: meaning, exact executable arithmetic, frame requirements and ###
# ###   resolution time. Nested names split by BALANCED X_ PREFIX (a last- ###
# ###   operator split produced garbage nodes); primitives RECURSE into    ###
# ###   their own requirements. Section 5 of every dossier entry carries   ###
# ###   the complete build.                                                ###
# ###                                                                      ###
# ###   BUILDER NOTE: two modules were silently DROPPED from earlier       ###
# ###   builds because the import-stripper orphaned a `try: import X`      ###
# ###   pair, leaving a dangling `except`. Both are now written without    ###
# ###   that pattern, and the builder verifies each module parses ALONE    ###
# ###   before embedding — a dropped module is reported, never silent.     ###
# ############################################################################

# ###                                                                      ###
# ###   v94 — THE FULLY DOCUMENTED DELIVERABLE (laz_export)                ###
# ###   Running the engine now writes an EIGHT-SHEET workbook in which     ###
# ###   every element is complete:                                         ###
# ###     01_STRATEGIES  every measured number + the full re-creation text ###
# ###     02_CONDITIONS  type, lineage, resolution, and HOW_TO_BUILD down  ###
# ###                    to primitives for every term in use               ###
# ###     03_PRIMITIVES  24 universal primitives: meaning, exact           ###
# ###                    arithmetic, requirements, resolution, and why     ###
# ###     04_BASES       every registry base with its arming rule          ###
# ###     05_DERIVED     manufactured conditions with parentage            ###
# ###     06_DOSSIER     long-form documentation, one block per strategy   ###
