# LAZ_BRAIN MODULE: laz_featdoc
# §laz_featdoc   <- grep this anchor to land here
# OBJECTIVE : FEATURE DOCUMENTATION TO PRIMITIVES
# PURPOSE   : Close the gap where strategies were fully documented but FEATURES were only registered. A production engineer had the lineage of X_u_pace__minus__u_time_in_lead but not the definition of either parent — those lived in a module docstring.
# HOW       : document_feature() walks any term down to PRIMITIVES, emitting for every node: meaning in words, exact executable arithmetic, what it requires from the frame, and when its value is DETERMINED. Nested manufactured names are split by BALANCED X_ PREFIX, not by last-operator (which produced garbage nodes). Primitives RECURSE into their own requirements, so u_margin_rate expands to u_margin and u_elapsed. Repeat visits are marked rather than duplicated.
# VALUE     : Section 5 of every dossier entry now carries the complete build. u_time_in_lead — which carries four of five tabletennis strategies — emits `(u_margin > 0).groupby(match).cumsum() / (cumcount() + 1)`. The dossier grew from ~45 to ~69 lines per strategy and no term requires reading source.
