"""laz_book.py — THE ENGINE CARRIES ITS OWN STRATEGIES.

WHAT WAS WRONG

Accepted strategies were written to mode3_<sport>_legs.csv and forgotten. The
next build knew nothing about them. Worse: once the register began suppressing
known strategies, that file was OVERWRITTEN with only the novel ones — 170
legs became 9 — so the most recent file no longer held the book at all.

Nothing was lost, but a book you cannot find is not a book, and a book the
engine does not carry is not knowledge. The engine already embeds its
recovered strategies, its master index, its production set and its book
stacks. Discovered strategies belong in exactly the same place.

WHAT THIS IS

An accumulating store, per sport, holding every strategy the engine has ever
validated — WITH ITS BASE AND ITS FULL CONDITION CHAIN, so it can be rebuilt
and placed without any other file:

    strategy_name · sport · base · conditions · odds · oos_win · oos_roi
    bets · tier · single_only · market · min_odds · resolves_at
    first_seen · runs_seen · origin_mode · engine_version

It is APPENDED, never overwritten. Deduped on the BET SET, because names
change between runs and bet sets do not. And it is EMBEDDED INTO THE ENGINE
at build time, so every future build starts holding everything learned so far.

THE RESET

reset() clears the suppression register — not the book. The engine then
re-derives from scratch and you can watch it rediscover what it knows, which
is the only honest way to check the book is still reachable. The strategies
themselves are never deleted by a reset.
"""
import os, json
import numpy as np, pandas as pd
laz_book__STORE = 'LAZ_BOOK.json'
